    "T2": {
      "text": "TF-IDF (term frequency-inverse document frequency) weights a word by how often it occurs in a document (term frequency) multiplied by its inverse document frequency, the log of the number of documents divided by the number of documents that contain the word. Words such as 'the' appear in most documents, so their IDF is low and they are down-weighted, while rare, discriminative words receive a higher weight.",
